2. Task 2: Repeated Substring Pattern – LeetCode
This problem can be solved elegantly using the KMP LPS (Longest Prefix Suffix) array.
Java Solution
class Solution {

    public boolean repeatedSubstringPattern(String s) {

        int n = s.length();

        int[] lps = new int[n];

        int len = 0;
        int i = 1;

        while (i < n) {

            if (s.charAt(i) == s.charAt(len)) {

                lps[i] = ++len;
                i++;

            } else if (len > 0) {

                len = lps[len - 1];

            } else {

                lps[i] = 0;
                i++;
            }
        }

        int longestPrefixSuffix = lps[n - 1];

        return longestPrefixSuffix > 0 &&
               n % (n - longestPrefixSuffix) == 0;
    }
}
Example
Input:
"abab"

Output:
true
Because:
"ab" + "ab" = "abab"
KMP Concept
For:
abab
LPS:
0 0 1 2
The longest prefix-suffix length is 2.
n - LPS = 4 - 2 = 2
Since:
4 % 2 = 0
the string consists of repeated substrings.
Time: O(n)
Space: O(n)
