3. KMP Applications
Task 3: Two Strings – HackerRank
The problem asks whether two strings share at least one common character.
A HashSet provides a simple efficient solution.
Java Solution
import java.util.*;

public class Solution {

    public static String twoStrings(String s1, String s2) {

        HashSet<Character> set = new HashSet<>();

        for (char c : s1.toCharArray()) {
            set.add(c);
        }

        for (char c : s2.toCharArray()) {

            if (set.contains(c)) {
                return "YES";
            }
        }

        return "NO";
    }
}
Example
s1 = "hello"
s2 = "world"

Output:
YES
Because both contain:
o
l
Time: O(n + m)
Space: O(Alphabet Size)
Teaching note: This task is listed under KMP Applications, but KMP is not necessary here because the problem only asks whether the strings share a character.
