5. Boyer-Moore Algorithm
Task 5: Mars Exploration – HackerRank
The expected repeated message is:
SOS
Count how many characters are different from the expected pattern.
Java Solution
import java.util.*;

public class Solution {

    public static int marsExploration(String s) {

        String pattern = "SOS";

        int changes = 0;

        for (int i = 0; i < s.length(); i++) {

            if (s.charAt(i) !=
                pattern.charAt(i % 3)) {

                changes++;
            }
        }

        return changes;
    }
}
Example
Input:
SOSSPSSQSSOR

Output:
3
Expected:
S O S S O S S O S S O S
Compare each character and count differences.
Time: O(n)
Space: O(1)
Teaching note: This HackerRank problem is not actually a Boyer-Moore string-search problem. It is a character-comparison problem. It can be used as a simple application exercise before teaching actual Boyer-Moore searching.
