7. Palindrome Techniques
Task 7: Palindrome Index – HackerRank
Find the index of the character that can be removed to make the string a palindrome.
Java Solution
public class Solution {

    public static int palindromeIndex(String s) {

        int left = 0;
        int right = s.length() - 1;

        while (left < right) {

            if (s.charAt(left) != s.charAt(right)) {

                if (isPalindrome(s, left + 1, right)) {
                    return left;
                }

                if (isPalindrome(s, left, right - 1)) {
                    return right;
                }

                return -1;
            }

            left++;
            right--;
        }

        return -1;
    }

    private static boolean isPalindrome(
            String s, int left, int right) {

        while (left < right) {

            if (s.charAt(left) != s.charAt(right)) {
                return false;
            }

            left++;
            right--;
        }

        return true;
    }
}
Example
Input:
aaab

Output:
3
Remove:
b
The remaining string:
aaa
is a palindrome.
Time: O(n)
Space: O(1)
